{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Origami’s patch graph and SwiftUI are both reactive dataflow, so the translator","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"targets SwiftUI’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"state graph","type":"text"}]},{"text":" — computed properties, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withAnimation"},{"text":" —","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not imperative functions. Each row below is a rule the codegen applies; the helper","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"library ("},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Drag"},{"type":"text","text":", …) fills the gaps where a patch has no direct"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"SwiftUI equivalent."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"The-four-rules","text":"The four rules","level":2},{"type":"table","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Origami"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"SwiftUI"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Pure value patch (Add, Transition\/interpolate, logic)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"computed property \/ expression"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Interaction (Tap, Down\/press, Double Tap, Long Press)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"gesture + "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@GestureState"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"origami.drag"},{"type":"text","text":" — Drag"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"drag(enable:momentum:bounds:position:translation:velocity:reset:)"},{"text":" (helper)","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"State\/memory (Switch, Sample and Hold)","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" + update logic","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Animation (Classic Animation, Pop\/Spring)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withAnimation"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".animation(.spring)"}]}]]],"header":"row"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The Origami layer tree becomes the SwiftUI "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"View"},{"type":"text","text":" body. Origami "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Transition"},{"type":"text","text":" means"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"interpolation (not SwiftUI’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".transition()"},{"type":"text","text":" modifier — that’s a different concept)."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Pure-value-patch-%E2%86%92-computed-property","text":"Pure value patch → computed property","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Add"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Transition\/interpolate"},{"type":"text","text":", and other pure-function patches carry no state."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"They fan an input through math and emit an output. In SwiftUI that’s a computed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"property (or an inline expression) — no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":", no side effect."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Interaction-%E2%86%92-gesture-+-State","text":"Interaction → gesture + `@State`","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Origami’s Interaction patch exposes discrete output ports: ","type":"text"},{"code":"down","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"position","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"onTap","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"onDoubleTap","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"onLongPress","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Each maps to a SwiftUI gesture recognizer","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whose output lands in ","type":"text"},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or fires a callback. The ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction","isActive":true},{"text":" helper","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"attaches only the recognizer for each output the caller requests, which keeps","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"gesture arbitration clean.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Statememory-%E2%86%92-State-+-update-logic","text":"State\/memory → `@State` + update logic","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Switch"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sample and Hold"},{"text":" remember a value across evaluations. That’s what","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"text":" is for. Codegen emits the state variable plus the update path (a gesture","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"callback, a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".onChange"},{"text":", or an assignment inside a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withAnimation"},{"text":" block).","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Animation-%E2%86%92-withAnimation--animation","text":"Animation → `withAnimation` \/ `.animation`","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"Classic Animation","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Pop Animation","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and other animation patches drive a value","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"toward a target over time. In SwiftUI, that’s a state change wrapped in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"withAnimation","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or an ","type":"text"},{"code":".animation(_:value:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" modifier on the animated property.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Continuous-time springs that don’t have a stock SwiftUI equivalent get flagged","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"by the parser — Swami won’t fake them.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Flag-dont-fake","text":"Flag, don’t fake","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Some Origami semantics don’t have a SwiftUI equivalent. When the parser hits one,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it emits a marker in the IR and codegen surfaces the gap rather than papering over","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it. The current list: continuous-time springs, custom JavaScript patches,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"absolute-position layout.","type":"text"}]}]}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/OrigamiMappings","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swami\/origamimappings"]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Reference","identifiers":["doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Beats"],"generated":true,"title":"Reference"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami"]]},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Swami"}],"title":"Origami → SwiftUI mappings"},"kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"How Swami translat